Original commit body from 3623397:

Before this change, running hypergumbo without the -t flag produced different
output than running with -t (bullet list structure vs tree format, no
Representativeness Table vs having one). This was confusing and indicated
deprecated code paths were still being used.

Changes:
- Default token budget to 4000 when -t is not specified (cli.py)
- Always create SketchStats for representativeness tracking
- Always use tree format for Structure section from the start
- Delete deprecated _format_structure() function
- Add directory type labels to tree fallback format
- Remove tests for deleted function

This ensures `hypergumbo .` produces the same output as `hypergumbo . -t 4000`.
